        "text": "The bear case on earnings quality is the one that matters. The bridge from $513M of GAAP net income to $769M of Adjusted EBITDA is clean, but the run-rate leans on reconditioning and logistics savings that management presents as structural. I would haircut the add-back stack by $95M in the base case, which is the difference between a net-cash balance sheet by mid-2027 and one a year later.",
